---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import {
  ChatSourcesCitationStates,
  ChatSourcesEmpty,
  ChatSourcesLongContent,
  ChatSourcesPlayground,
  ChatSourcesSingle,
  ChatSourcesWithCitations,
} from '../../components/ChatSourcesDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Chat Sources"
  description="Numbered citations, citations checked on open, and the list of sources a reply used."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Chat Sources</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows where a reply came from. Hovering or clicking a citation previews the cited passage and its source. Checked
    citations recheck access each time they open, and a count opens the list of every source the reply used.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ChatSourcesPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Numbered citations and a sources list"
      code={`import { ChatSources, InlineCitation, type ChatSource } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chat-sources";

const sources: ChatSource[] = [
  {
    id: "checklist",
    title: "Supplier onboarding checklist",
    location: "Note · Before the first order",
    excerpt: "Collect the W-9 and bank details before the first purchase order.",
    href: "/notes/checklist",
  },
];

<p>
  Collect the tax form first. <InlineCitation source={sources[0]} number={1} />
</p>
<ChatSources sources={sources} />`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>ChatSource</code>: <code>{'{ id, title, location, excerpt, href }'}</code>.<code>href</code> opens in a
        new tab.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>InlineCitation</code>: <code>source</code> and its
        <code>number</code>. It is a small secondary icon button.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>ChatSources</code>: <code>sources</code> in citation order, and
        <code>defaultOpen</code> to start with the list open.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>CheckedCitation</code>: the linked <code>label</code>, a<code>state</code>, <code>onOpen</code> (called on
        every open), and
        <code>onRetry</code>. It is a link button that wraps with the text.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Inline citations and sources</h2>
    <p>
      Numbers in the reply match the numbered list. Each citation and each list item shows the title, where it lives,
      the passage, and an “Open source” link.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChatSourcesWithCitations client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">One source</h2>
    <p>The count reads “1 source”. The list starts closed.</p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChatSourcesSingle client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Empty sources</h2>
    <p>With no sources, it says none were used.</p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChatSourcesEmpty client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Checked citations</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>CheckedCitation</code> when a source can change or access can end. Your app checks access in{' '}
      <code>onOpen</code> and passes the result as <code>state</code>. A removed source shows why, never its old
      passage. A failed check offers “Load source again”.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      code={`type CitationState =
  | { kind: "idle" } | { kind: "loading" }
  | { kind: "ready"; title: string; location: string; excerpt: string }
  | { kind: "unavailable"; message: string }
  | { kind: "error"; message: string };

<MessageResponse
  renderLink={(href, label) =>
    isCitation(href)
      ? <CheckedCitation label={text(label)} state={state} onOpen={check} onRetry={check} />
      : <a href={href}>{label}</a>}
>
  {reply}
</MessageResponse>`}
    />
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChatSourcesCitationStates client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Long content</h2>
    <p>Long file names, paths, and links wrap inside a narrow chat.</p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChatSourcesLongContent client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Inline citations are named “Source 1: title”; checked citations “Source: label”. Both open a popover after a 300ms
      hover, on click or tap, or with Enter or Space. The pointer can move into the popover to reach “Open source”.
      Escape closes it and returns focus. The sources count is a disclosure button with
      <code>aria-expanded</code>, and the list is ordered. “Open source” tells screen readers it opens a new tab.
    </p>
    <p>
      Checking access is announced as a status; unavailable and error messages as alerts. After “Load source again”,
      focus stays in the popover. Colors change over 120ms and the list grows over 180ms; with reduced motion both
      change at once.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Cards use <code>--sprout-line</code> and <code>--sprout-surface</code>, secondary text <code>--sprout-muted</code>
      , and links
      <code>--sprout-primary</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
